  "slug": "skip-lists",
    "markdown": "# Skip Lists: Probabilistic Linked Indexing & Express Lanes\n\n![Skip Lists: Probabilistic Linked Indexing & Express Lanes](/images/dsa/skip-lists-dark.jpg#dark)\n\nWhile linked lists excel at insertion, searching them requires linear scans ($O(N)$). To speed up searches on linked structures without the balancing code of AVL trees, we use **Skip Lists**.\n\nThis chapter explores **Skip Lists**. We focus on probabilistic node levels (express lanes), search traversal bounds, and database sorting indexes.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Multi-Level Express Lanes Search Paths\n\nA skip list consists of a base linked list containing all elements, topped by a series of **express lane** layers. Each higher level skips elements in the layers below, creating shortcuts.\n\n```\nLevel 2: [Head] --------------> [30] -----------------------------> null\nLevel 1: [Head] ------> [15] -> [30] --------------> [50] --------> null\nLevel 0: [Head] -> [5] -> [15] -> [30] -> [42] -> [50] -> [60] -> null\n```\n\nTo search for a target (e.g. 42):\n1. Start at the top level.\n2. Walk forward until the next node is larger than the target (or null).\n3. Drop down a level and repeat.\n4. Continue until you find the target or reach the base level.\n\n### Multi-Level express search paths\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <rect width=\"600\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#27272a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"35\" fill=\"#a855f7\" font-size=\"13\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\">Skip List Search Express Lanes</text>\n\n  <g transform=\"translate(45, 60)\">\n    {/* Level 1: Express */}\n    <text x=\"0\" y=\"15\" fill=\"#a855f7\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"monospace\">L1 Express</text>\n    <rect x=\"70\" y=\"5\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#a855f7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"90\" y=\"17\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">10</text>\n    <rect x=\"210\" y=\"5\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#a855f7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"230\" y=\"17\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">30</text>\n    \n    <path d=\"M 110,15 L 205,15\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#a855f7\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-skip-lanes)\"/>\n\n    {/* Level 0: Base */}\n    <text x=\"0\" y=\"55\" fill=\"#71717a\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"monospace\">L0 Base</text>\n    <rect x=\"70\" y=\"45\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n    <text x=\"90\" y=\"57\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">10</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"45\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n    <text x=\"160\" y=\"57\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">20</text>\n    <rect x=\"210\" y=\"45\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n    <text x=\"230\" y=\"57\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">30</text>\n\n    <path d=\"M 110,55 L 135,55\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-skip-lanes-blue)\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 180,55 L 205,55\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-skip-lanes-blue)\"/>\n\n    {/* Drop-down path */}\n    <path d=\"M 230,25 L 230,40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 1\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-skip-lanes-red)\"/>\n    <text x=\"250\" y=\"35\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"monospace\">Drop Down</text>\n  </g>\n\n  <defs>\n    <marker id=\"arrow-skip-lanes\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"4\" markerHeight=\"4\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" fill=\"#a855f7\" />\n    </marker>\n    <marker id=\"arrow-skip-lanes-blue\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"4\" markerHeight=\"4\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" />\n    </marker>\n    <marker id=\"arrow-skip-lanes-red\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"4\" markerHeight=\"4\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" fill=\"#ef4444\" />\n    </marker>\n  </defs>\n</svg>\n\nBecause we halve the search space at each level, searches run in $O(\\log N)$ average complexity, matches tree lookup speeds using plain references.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Probabilistic Balancing: Coin Flips Growth\n\nWhen inserting a node, how do we decide which levels it should belong to? Instead of strict balancing codes:\n1. Insert the node at the base level.\n2. Flip a coin (generate a random float $\\in [0, 1)$).\n3. If it is heads (value $< 0.5$), promote the node to Level 1.\n4. Flip again. If heads, promote it to Level 2.\n5. Repeat until tails.\n\n### Node Promotion Checks\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <rect width=\"600\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#27272a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"35\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"13\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\">Probabilistic Node Level Promotion</text>\n\n  <g transform=\"translate(45, 60)\">\n    {/* Base Node */}\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"45\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"40\" y=\"64\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">Base: Level 0</text>\n\n    {/* Coin flip path */}\n    <path d=\"M 90,60 L 175,60\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-skip-coin)\"/>\n    <text x=\"130\" y=\"52\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"8\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">Coin: Heads</text>\n\n    {/* Promoted Node */}\n    <g transform=\"translate(190, 10)\">\n      <rect x=\"0\" y=\"35\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n      <text x=\"40\" y=\"54\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">Level 1</text>\n      <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n      <text x=\"40\" y=\"19\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">Level 0</text>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n\n  <defs>\n    <marker id=\"arrow-skip-coin\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"4\" markerHeight=\"4\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" fill=\"#10b981\" />\n    </marker>\n  </defs>\n</svg>\n\n---\n\n## 3. Practice Checklist\n\n### Beginner Problems\n* [Design Skiplist (LeetCode 1206)](https://leetcode.com/problems/design-skiplist/): Build multi-level index.\n  * *Why this is useful:* Master coordinate-like node adjustments and random level assignment loops.\n* [Linked List Cycle (LeetCode 141)](https://leetcode.com/problems/linked-list-cycle/): Cycle searches.\n  * *Why this is useful:* Build core link cycle parsing skills.\n",
