      "summary": "The Gilbert-Johnson-Keerthi (GJK) algorithm determines whether two convex shapes overlap by iteratively building a simplex in the Minkowski Difference space. If the origin lies within the Minkowski Difference, the shapes overlap. GJK is the industry standard for convex-convex collision detection in game physics engines."
