      "summary": "The Rendering Equation (Kajiya 1986) is the fundamental mathematical framework describing how light interacts with surfaces. It states that outgoing radiance equals emitted radiance plus the integral of incoming radiance weighted by the BRDF over the hemisphere — all physically-based rendering (PBR) techniques are approximations of this equation."
