      "summary": "Texture mapping applies 2D images (textures) to 3D surfaces by mapping surface points to texture coordinates (UV coordinates). Beyond simple color mapping, games use normal maps, metallic-roughness maps, emissive maps, and displacement maps to add detail, physical material properties, and depth to surfaces at low polygon cost."
