    "markdown": "# Computer Graphics: GLSL (OpenGL Shading Language)\n\n**GLSL (OpenGL Shading Language)** is the cross-platform shading language designed to write GPU programs for the OpenGL and WebGL graphics APIs. It is highly integrated with Unix-like operating systems, Linux, macOS, Android, and web browsers.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Syntax, Bindings & Modern Keywords\n\nGLSL shares C-style syntax but uses distinct keywords for parameter routing between pipeline stages.\n\n### 1.1 Attribute and Varying Routing\nIn older GLSL versions, variable bindings used legacy keywords (`attribute` and `varying`). Modern GLSL (version 330 core+) replaces these with clear inputs and outputs:\n*   **`in`:** Declares an incoming variable (input attributes from vertex buffers, or inputs to a fragment shader from the rasterizer).\n*   **`out`:** Declares an outgoing variable (output from vertex shader, or output target color from fragment shader).\n*   **`uniform`:** Declares global parameters set by the CPU that remain constant across all threads in a draw call.\n\n### 1.2 Layout Location Bindings\nTo associate vertex buffer data directly with shader input attributes without query calls on the CPU, GLSL uses **Layout Qualifiers**:\n\n```glsl\nlayout (location = 0) in vec3 aPos;     // Maps to vertex buffer stream 0\nlayout (location = 1) in vec3 aNormal;  // Maps to vertex buffer stream 1\nlayout (location = 2) in vec2 aTexCoords;\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Compilation Architectures: GLSL vs. HLSL\n\nUnlike HLSL (which is pre-compiled to bytecode offline), traditional OpenGL pipelines compile GLSL **at runtime** inside the graphics driver:\n\n<div style=\"margin: 20px 0; text-align: center;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 220\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\" style=\"background: #141416; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #27272a;\">\n  <!-- Traditional GLSL Path -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(10, 0)\">\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"30\" width=\"130\" height=\"35\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n    <text x=\"35\" y=\"52\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Raw GLSL (Text)</text>\n    \n    <line x1=\"155\" y1=\"47\" x2=\"195\" y2=\"47\" stroke=\"#71717a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-zinc)\" />\n    \n    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"25\" width=\"130\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n    <text x=\"210\" y=\"52\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"10\">Driver Compiler</text>\n    \n    <line x1=\"335\" y1=\"47\" x2=\"375\" y2=\"47\" stroke=\"#71717a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-zinc)\" />\n    \n    <rect x=\"380\" y=\"30\" width=\"90\" height=\"35\" fill=\"#10b981\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n    <text x=\"390\" y=\"52\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">GPU Binary</text>\n    \n    <text x=\"20\" y=\"85\" fill=\"#71717a\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\">Traditional: Driver compiles raw text on game load (Slow)</text>\n  </g>\n  \n  <!-- Modern SPIR-V Path -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(10, 100)\">\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"30\" width=\"130\" height=\"35\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n    <text x=\"35\" y=\"52\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Pre-compiled GLSL</text>\n    \n    <line x1=\"155\" y1=\"47\" x2=\"195\" y2=\"47\" stroke=\"#71717a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-zinc)\" />\n    \n    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"30\" width=\"130\" height=\"35\" fill=\"#10b981\" fill-opacity=\"0.15\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"3\" />\n    <text x=\"215\" y=\"52\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11\">SPIR-V Bytecode</text>\n    \n    <line x1=\"335\" y1=\"47\" x2=\"375\" y2=\"47\" stroke=\"#71717a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-zinc)\" />\n    \n    <rect x=\"380\" y=\"30\" width=\"90\" height=\"35\" fill=\"#10b981\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n    <text x=\"390\" y=\"52\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">GPU Binary</text>\n    \n    <text x=\"20\" y=\"85\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\">Vulkan: Pre-compiled offline -> Driver loads instantly (Fast)</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 3. Implementation Example: GLSL Shaders\n\nHere is a GLSL shader pair implementing standard diffuse and specular Blinn-Phong lighting:\n\n```glsl\n// --- VERTEX SHADER ROUTINE ---\n#version 330 core\nlayout (location = 0) in vec3 aPos;\nlayout (location = 1) in vec3 aNormal;\nlayout (location = 2) in vec2 aTexCoords;\n\nout vec3 FragPos;\nout vec3 Normal;\nout vec2 TexCoords;\n\nuniform mat4 model;\nuniform mat4 view;\nuniform mat4 projection;\n\nvoid main()\n{\n    // Compute world space fragment coordinate\n    FragPos = vec3(model * vec4(aPos, 1.0));\n    \n    // Transform normal vector (ignoring non-uniform scale shear using normal matrix)\n    Normal = mat3(transpose(inverse(model))) * aNormal;\n    \n    TexCoords = aTexCoords;\n    \n    // Output position to clip space\n    gl_Position = projection * view * vec4(FragPos, 1.0);\n}\n\n// --- FRAGMENT SHADER ROUTINE ---\n#version 330 core\nout vec4 FragColor;\n\nin vec3 FragPos;\nin vec3 Normal;\nin vec2 TexCoords;\n\nuniform vec3 lightPos;\nuniform vec3 viewPos;\nuniform vec3 lightColor;\n\nuniform sampler2D texture_diffuse;\n\nvoid main()\n{\n    // 1. Normal and light directions\n    vec3 norm = normalize(Normal);\n    vec3 lightDir = normalize(lightPos - FragPos);\n    \n    // 2. Diffuse shading (Lambertian)\n    float diff = max(dot(norm, lightDir), 0.0);\n    vec3 diffuse = diff * lightColor;\n    \n    // 3. Specular shading (Blinn-Phong)\n    vec3 viewDir = normalize(viewPos - FragPos);\n    vec3 halfwayDir = normalize(lightDir + viewDir);\n    float spec = pow(max(dot(norm, halfwayDir), 0.0), 32.0); // 32.0: shininess exponent\n    vec3 specular = spec * lightColor;\n    \n    // 4. Sample diffuse texture and combine\n    vec3 texColor = texture(texture_diffuse, TexCoords).rgb;\n    vec3 result = (diffuse + specular) * texColor;\n    \n    FragColor = vec4(result, 1.0);\n}\n```\n",
