  "slug": "game-ai-decision-tree",
    "markdown": "# Game AI: Decision Trees\n\nA **Decision Tree** is a hierarchical, predictive model used in game AI to select actions for NPCs (Non-Player Characters). By structure, it is a tree of nodes where internal nodes evaluate game state variables, and leaf nodes contain final character actions.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Structure & Traversal Mechanics\n\nEvaluation begins at the **Root Node** and runs top-down:\n1.  **Branch Nodes (Decision Points):** Each branch evaluates a condition (e.g., `health < 30`, `hasAmmo == true`). Based on the boolean result, traversal forks down the matching child link.\n2.  **Leaf Nodes (Action Points):** Once traversal reaches a leaf node, the corresponding action is executed (e.g., `Attack`, `FindCover`, `Idle`).\n\n### Advantages:\n*   **Performance:** Traversing a tree is extremely fast, requiring $O(D)$ operations (where $D$ is the maximum depth of the tree).\n*   **Simplicity:** Easy to construct, understand, and debug compared to complex neural networks.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Decision Tree vs. Behavior Tree\n\nIt is important not to confuse Decision Trees with modern **Behavior Trees**:\n\n| Feature | Decision Tree | Behavior Tree |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Control Flow** | Purely conditional branches. | Sequencers, Selectors, and Decorators. |\n| **State Tracking** | Stateless (runs top-down in a single pass). | State-aware (supports `RUNNING`, `SUCCESS`, `FAILURE` node return status). |\n| **Action Execution** | Instantly selects one action per frame. | Actions can run over multiple frames (e.g., pathfinding to a target). |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Visual Representation\n\nBelow is a decision tree for a basic guard patrol agent:\n\n<div style=\"margin: 20px 0; text-align: center;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 240\" width=\"100%\" height=\"240\" style=\"background: #141416; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #27272a;\">\n  <!-- Root Node (Enemies Nearby?) -->\n  <rect x=\"180\" y=\"20\" width=\"140\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n  <text x=\"195\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"10\">Enemy Nearby?</text>\n  \n  <!-- Left path (Yes) -->\n  <path d=\"M 200 60 L 140 100\" stroke=\"#71717a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <text x=\"145\" y=\"75\" fill=\"#a1a1aa\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">Yes</text>\n  \n  <!-- Right path (No) -> Leaf (Patrol) -->\n  <path d=\"M 300 60 L 360 100\" stroke=\"#71717a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <text x=\"335\" y=\"75\" fill=\"#a1a1aa\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">No</text>\n  <rect x=\"310\" y=\"100\" width=\"100\" height=\"35\" fill=\"#10b981\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n  <text x=\"340\" y=\"122\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Patrol</text>\n  \n  <!-- Left Branch (Low Health?) -->\n  <rect x=\"70\" y=\"100\" width=\"140\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n  <text x=\"95\" y=\"125\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"10\">Low Health?</text>\n  \n  <!-- Left path of Left Branch (Yes) -> Leaf (Flee) -->\n  <path d=\"M 100 140 L 60 180\" stroke=\"#71717a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <text x=\"65\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#a1a1aa\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">Yes</text>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"180\" width=\"100\" height=\"35\" fill=\"#f43f5e\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#f43f5e\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n  <text x=\"45\" y=\"202\" fill=\"#f43f5e\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Flee</text>\n  \n  <!-- Right path of Left Branch (No) -> Leaf (Attack) -->\n  <path d=\"M 180 140 L 220 180\" stroke=\"#71717a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" />\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#a1a1aa\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">No</text>\n  <rect x=\"170\" y=\"180\" width=\"100\" height=\"35\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"3\" />\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"202\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">Attack</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 4. Implementation Example (Python - Class-based Decision Tree)\n\n```python\nclass DecisionNode:\n    def evaluate(self, agent_state):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\nclass DecisionBranch(DecisionNode):\n    def __init__(self, condition_func, true_node, false_node):\n        self.condition_func = condition_func\n        self.true_node = true_node\n        self.false_node = false_node\n        \n    def evaluate(self, agent_state):\n        # Evaluate conditional function and traverse\n        if self.condition_func(agent_state):\n            return self.true_node.evaluate(agent_state)\n        else:\n            return self.false_node.evaluate(agent_state)\n\nclass ActionLeaf(DecisionNode):\n    def __init__(self, action_name):\n        self.action_name = action_name\n        \n    def evaluate(self, agent_state):\n        # Base leaf case returns the chosen action\n        return self.action_name\n\n# --- Example Usage ---\n# State Dictionary\nguard_state = {\n    \"enemy_nearby\": True,\n    \"health\": 25\n}\n\n# Define Nodes\nflee_action = ActionLeaf(\"FLEE\")\nattack_action = ActionLeaf(\"ATTACK\")\npatrol_action = ActionLeaf(\"PATROL\")\n\n# Define Branches\nhealth_branch = DecisionBranch(lambda state: state[\"health\"] < 30, flee_action, attack_action)\nroot_branch = DecisionBranch(lambda state: state[\"enemy_nearby\"], health_branch, patrol_action)\n\n# Traverse Decision Tree\nselected_action = root_branch.evaluate(guard_state)\nprint(\"AI Decided Action:\", selected_action) # Output: FLEE\n```\n",
    "title": "Game AI: Decision Trees",
    "tagline": "Hierarchical conditional node evaluation structures and decision vs behavior trees.",
