  "slug": "game-ai-markov",
    "markdown": "# Game AI: Markov Chains & Probabilistic Behaviors\n\nA **Markov Chain** is a mathematical model representing a state machine where transitions between states are determined by probability calculations. It is used in game AI to generate organic, less predictable variations in NPC behaviors (such as idle animations, fighting patterns, or weather cycles).\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Markov Property (Memorylessness)\n\nThe defining characteristic of a Markov Chain is the **Markov Property**: the probability of transitioning to the next state depends **solely** on the current state, completely ignoring previous historical sequences:\n\n$$P(S_{t+1} = s \\mid S_t = s_t, S_{t-1} = s_{t-1}, \\dots, S_0 = s_0) = P(S_{t+1} = s \\mid S_t = s_t)$$\n\n---\n\n## 2. The Transition Probability Matrix\n\nA Markov Chain is defined by a **Transition Matrix ($P$)**, where each entry $P_{ij}$ represents the probability of transitioning from current state $i$ to next state $j$:\n\n$$P = \\begin{pmatrix}\nP_{00} & P_{01} & P_{02} \\\\\nP_{10} & P_{11} & P_{12} \\\\\nP_{20} & P_{21} & P_{22}\n\\end{pmatrix}$$\n\n*   **Constraint:** Because the system must transition to *some* state in the next step, the sum of probabilities across any horizontal row **must equal exactly $1.0$**:\n    $$\\sum_{j} P_{ij} = 1.0$$\n\n---\n\n## 3. Visual State Transition Representation\n\nBelow is a state transition graph representing a guard NPC's patrol variation:\n\n<div style=\"margin: 20px 0; text-align: center;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 220\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\" style=\"background: #141416; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #27272a;\">\n  <!-- State: Idle -->\n  <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"110\" r=\"30\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"2\" />\n  <text x=\"80\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11\">Idle</text>\n  \n  <!-- State: Patrol -->\n  <circle cx=\"400\" cy=\"110\" r=\"30\" fill=\"#10b981\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" />\n  <text x=\"375\" y=\"115\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"11\">Patrol</text>\n  \n  <!-- Self Loop: Idle (P = 0.4) -->\n  <path d=\"M 85 85 A 20 20 0 1 1 115 85\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-blue)\" />\n  <text x=\"90\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">P = 0.4</text>\n  \n  <!-- Self Loop: Patrol (P = 0.7) -->\n  <path d=\"M 385 85 A 20 20 0 1 1 415 85\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-emerald)\" />\n  <text x=\"390\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"9\">P = 0.7</text>\n  \n  <!-- Transition Idle -> Patrol (P = 0.6) -->\n  <path d=\"M 130 95 Q 250 65 370 95\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-amber)\" />\n  <text x=\"235\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">P = 0.6</text>\n  \n  <!-- Transition Patrol -> Idle (P = 0.3) -->\n  <path d=\"M 370 125 Q 250 155 130 125\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-amber)\" />\n  <text x=\"235\" y=\"150\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">P = 0.3</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 4. Implementation Example (Python - Matrix Solver)\n\n```python\nimport random\n\nclass MarkovChainAI:\n    def __init__(self, states, transition_matrix):\n        self.states = states\n        # transition_matrix: dict of dicts, e.g. {\"IDLE\": {\"IDLE\": 0.4, \"PATROL\": 0.6}}\n        self.matrix = transition_matrix\n        self.current_state = states[0]\n        \n    def step(self):\n        # 1. Get probability distributions for the current state\n        transitions = self.matrix[self.current_state]\n        \n        # 2. Pick a random number between 0 and 1\n        rand_val = random.random()\n        cumulative_probability = 0.0\n        \n        # 3. Select next state based on cumulative weight ranges\n        for next_state, probability in transitions.items():\n            cumulative_probability += probability\n            if rand_val <= cumulative_probability:\n                self.current_state = next_state\n                break\n                \n        return self.current_state\n\n# --- Simulation setup ---\nstates_list = [\"IDLE\", \"PATROL\"]\ntrans_table = {\n    \"IDLE\":   {\"IDLE\": 0.4, \"PATROL\": 0.6},\n    \"PATROL\": {\"IDLE\": 0.3, \"PATROL\": 0.7}\n}\n\nai = MarkovChainAI(states_list, trans_table)\n\n# Run 10 ticks of the Markov Chain\nhistory = []\nfor _ in range(10):\n    history.append(ai.step())\nprint(\"AI State History:\", \" -> \".join(history))\n```\n",
    "title": "Game AI: Markov Chains & Probabilistic Behaviors",
    "tagline": "Memoryless Markov property, probability transition matrices, and randomized NPC behaviors.",
    "category": "Game Developer",
    "readTime": 15,
